WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.150
Each legacy group then lands
in one of four patterns.

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:08.712
Pattern one: organization-derived groups,
kept from the org chart, become dynamic.

3
00:00:08.712 --> 00:00:13.741
The kit writes the rule on the H R
organization code in extension attribute ten,

4
00:00:13.741 --> 00:00:18.151
with clauses that require an enabled
account and a member, not a guest.

5
00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:20.387
Never on department or job title.

6
00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:24.859
Pattern two: explicit role groups
become assigned, managed by a delegated

7
00:00:24.859 --> 00:00:27.645
administrator, and
eligible through pim when

8
00:00:27.645 --> 00:00:30.284
the group holds sys-admin
or security admin.

9
00:00:30.284 --> 00:00:33.437
Pattern three: distribution
lists become mail-only.

10
00:00:33.437 --> 00:00:37.863
Update the Sequel Server Agent operator's
address, and give it no login.

11
00:00:37.863 --> 00:00:42.130
Pattern four: mail-enabled security
groups split in two, a mail-only group

12
00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:46.825
and an assigned security group, with the
pairing recorded in both descriptions.

13
00:00:46.825 --> 00:00:49.088
And when a group's codes aren't recorded,

14
00:00:49.088 --> 00:00:52.630
the target says to ask H R for
the code before writing the rule.
